  "changes": [
    "Both raw XML admission passes now track open-element depth against the existing 256-level ODG limit immediately after each borrowed Start or virtual Empty event; only the bounded max-plus-one quick-xml open-name state can exist before refusal, rather than an unbounded stack.",
    "The package and Flat depth guards preserve quick-xml check_end_names and leave ordinary malformed/end-name diagnostics to the existing resolver/parser after bounded admission.",
    "Added a public FlatDrawing allocation probe with eight million nested elements; it refuses at the depth limit before the reader can grow a large open-name stack and keeps observed post-input allocations below 32 MiB.",
    "Documented the intentional Flat UTF-8-before-detector ordering: invalid UTF-8 retains a direct typed source error, while raw admission still precedes the detector because detector namespace resolution can own oversized root declarations."
  ],
  "normative": {
    "depth_admission": "Raw admission enforces MAX_DEPTH=256 before requesting another event beyond the one current start state quick-xml has already opened; valid inputs at or below the limit retain existing check_end_names behavior. Empty events are checked at their virtual depth without growing the open-name stack.",
    "allocation_probe": "The public deep-nesting probe constructs 8,000,000 nested <x> elements and asserts typed nesting refusal plus a bounded allocation envelope.",
